      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e It is also unfortunate that we need this extra annotation. Note that `new_size` is assigned to `bw-\u003emax_pos` in the next line, so we still satisfy the annotaton in src/utils/bit_writer_utils.h that `buf` is sized by `max_pos`.\n\n\nI think that\u0027s touched on in the commit message:\n\nThis annotation introduced a new build error in the `BitWriterResize`\nfunction (`src/utils/bit_writer_utils.c`, lines 53-54) when assigning\nthe result of `WebPSafeMalloc` (an `__unsafe_indexable` pointer) to the\nnow-annotated `bw-\u003ebuf`. This was resolved by:\n1. Casting `bw-\u003ebuf` to `(uint8_t* __unsafe_indexable)` before passing\n   it to `WEBP_UNSAFE_MEMCPY` (line 50) and `WebPSafeFree` (line 52).\n2. Using `bw-\u003ebuf \u003d __unsafe_forge_bidi_indexable(uint8_t*, new_buf,\n   new_size);` (line 53) to create a properly bounded pointer from the\n  `malloc` result (`new_buf`) using its size (`new_size`) before\n  assigning it to `bw-\u003ebuf`.",
      "parentUuid": "f5f655ee_37605b0c",
